Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): And then, let's say, when these guys, for instance, invoke this API, it's called Send Raw Transaction, which is the one through which most of these clients will request the invocation of a smart contract. What we do inside is we spin up the CVM, we execute the transaction, and then somehow.

