Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): And that's the touch point with Fabric, because out of the execution, we don't persist, right?

109
00:15:52.540 --> 00:16:03.370
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): we actually get a read-write set out of it. And then the rest is purely fabric, because then we're gonna have endorsement, ordering, finality, so stuff that fabric knows. So this is really the touch point.

