00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:37.850
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): And it will do so through the state DB.

121
00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:44.869
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): And we provide, actually, a StateDB wrapper to the EVM, not the original one.

122
00:17:45.660 --> 00:18:00.529
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): And this State DB wrapper will do a bunch of things. It will… well, so it will… first of all, it will wrap the fabric world state, so this DB here is either Fabric or Fabric X's world state, and ways to access that.

