00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:20.830
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): And we're also gonna register a write, because we don't persist them immediately, and as I said, as I anticipated earlier, we were gonna construct read-write sets for that.

125
00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:29.219
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): Then we have also chain config and block context, because we need to provide a full execution context for the EVM.

126
00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:42.159
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): And then finally, architecturally, we have this fabric connector, which takes care of all that follows the execution, so endorsing, ordering, committing, checking for finality.

