00:45:10.810 --> 00:45:14.569
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): We'll be on this side of the house.

342
00:45:14.610 --> 00:45:32.889
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): So, if, I mean, if we go with what, what was suggested before, and, you know, we just have, we handle NVCC conflicts with retries, that's not going to be a problem. It's something you can, you can just easily do, but then, I mean, if you… we might realize that for some workloads.

343
00:45:32.950 --> 00:45:43.300
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): performance degrades. And again, performance, we should keep in mind that, we… depending on the L1 we're comparing with,

