00:45:43.710 --> 00:45:48.300
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): No matter what, we might still be exceeding expectations.

345
00:45:48.410 --> 00:45:53.389
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): But still, if we want to do better, and we want to implement some kind of dependency graph.

346
00:45:53.760 --> 00:46:08.679
Alessandro Sorniotti (IBM): and we want to have an endorsement policy that says that I need a majority of endorsers, then you're in the business of implementing a distributed dependency graph, which is something that is doable, but it adds to the complexity and footprint of the system.

347
00:46:08.990 --> 00:46:10.010
Marcus Brandenburger (IBM Research Zurich): Right.

348
00:46:11.230 --> 00:46:25.649
